CONTRIBUTORS:

Jon Tiritilli (Original Author):
- Original LifePuck hardware integration and driver development
- Core life counter implementation (single and two-player)
- LVGL framework setup and display driver
- Battery management, audio system, RTC integration
- Initial preset system and menu structure
- Hardware abstraction layer for ESP32-S3 Touch LCD 1.85"

Pascal "Suthe" (2025):
- Complete Theme System Implementation:
  - 5 themes with custom background images (Yugioh, Magic, Pokemon, Default, Off)
  - Automatic theme mode with preset-based assignment
  - Manual theme selection with live updates
  - Theme integration across all UI elements (buttons, icons, text)
  
- Centralized Configuration System:
  - New config.h as single source of truth (89 configurable values)
  - Force reset flags for testing and deployment (9 flags, fully functional)
  - Touch calibration defaults centralized from hardcoded values
  - All preset definitions moved to config.h for easy editing
  
- Touch Calibration Enhancements:
  - "Suthe's Method" - Interactive zone-based calibration algorithm
  - Power management suspension during calibration (prevents interruptions)
  - Two-pass system (coarse + fine) for speed and precision
  - Comprehensive calibration documentation
  
- Preset Editor Enhancements:
  - Theme selection available for ALL presets (not just custom)
  - Per-preset theme overrides with NVS persistence
  - Scrolling support with proper layout (5-row grid)
  - All preset values editable on-device
  
- Bug Fixes and Improvements:
  - Touch calibration no longer interrupted by auto-dim/sleep
  - Theme backgrounds refresh immediately on Life Counter return
  - Preset changes trigger live theme updates in Automatic mode
  - Theme text colors with proper contrast on all backgrounds
  - Consistent time units throughout configuration
  
- Documentation:
  - Suthe's Method calibration algorithm documentation
  - Display coordinate system documentation updates
  - Configuration system documentation
  - Comprehensive inline code comments
